  "question": "Business requirements description of catering management system: The system is used to manage the daily operation of the restaurant, covering functions such as user management, dish management, order processing, and sales statistics. The system contains multiple users, each of whom has a username, password, and role, and the roles are divided into customers and administrators. The system records multiple dishes, each of which has the name, price, category, and availability status, and supports the management of dishes on and off the shelves. Customers can place orders, and each order has an order ID, order user ID, order time, total order amount, and order status. The order status includes pending, in progress, and completed. Each order contains multiple dishes, and the order details record the order ID, dish ID, and quantity to ensure the integrity of the order information. The system also supports sales statistics, recording the total sales quantity and total sales by date and dish, which is convenient for restaurants to conduct business analysis. Through user tables, dish tables, order tables, order details tables, and statistical tables, the system realizes comprehensive management of restaurant operations and ensures the accuracy and traceability of data.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0429\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_users_username` (`username`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `dishes` (\n  `dish_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `dish_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `availability_status` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`dish_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `orders` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `total_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  KEY `idx_orders_user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `orders_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_details` (\n  `order_detail_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `dish_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_detail_id`),\n  KEY `idx_order_details_order_id` (`order_id`),\n  KEY `idx_order_details_dish_id` (`dish_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_details_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `orders` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_details_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`dish_id`) REFERENCES `dishes` (`dish_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_statistics` (\n  `stat_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `stat_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `dish_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_sales_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_sales_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`stat_id`),\n  KEY `idx_sales_statistics_dish_id` (`dish_id`),\n  KEY `idx_sales_statistics_stat_date` (`stat_date`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_statistics_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`dish_id`) REFERENCES `dishes` (`dish_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
